course: dictionary
lesson: 9144
title: Sneeze: a word that tickles
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To sneeze means to suddenly blow air out through your nose and mouth with a loud noise, because something tickles inside your nose. A sneeze is the act or sound of sneezing, so the word can be a verb («Pepper makes me sneeze») or a noun («A sneeze can spray droplets several metres»).
explain: Use the context to check the meaning. «Colds and flu are caused by viruses, tiny germs that travel in the drops we sneeze and cough out» tells you that sneezing sends germs into the air. The words around sneeze give you the clues.
explain: Sneezing also teaches manners and science. People say «Bless you!» after someone sneezes, which is a polite thing to do. Sneezing is a reflex, so your body does it without you deciding.
fact: To sneeze means to blow air out suddenly through your nose and mouth with a loud noise.
fact: A sneeze is the act or sound of sneezing.
fact: A sneeze can spray droplets several metres, so catch it in a tissue or sneeze into your elbow.
fact: «Catch it, bin it, kill it» means: catch the sneeze in a tissue, throw the tissue away, then wash your hands.
fact: Sneezing is a reflex: your body does it without you deciding.
exercise: «Air is full of tiny specks of dust, and pollen makes people with hay fever sneeze.» What does sneeze mean here? | *To blow air suddenly out of your nose and mouth with a loud noise | To shine brightly like a sunbeam | To fall asleep quickly | To sing a soft lullaby
exercise: What is the best way to stop germs spreading when you sneeze? | Hold your breath and wait for it to pass | *Sneeze into a tissue or your elbow, bin the tissue, then wash your hands | Sneeze into the air and walk away | Sneeze on the things you touch so you can share the germs
exercise: Why do people say «Bless you!» when someone sneezes? | To wake the sneezer up | To make the sneeze stop | *To be polite and show they care | To ask for a tissue
test: «The sneeze was so loud that the cat jumped.» In this sentence, what is a sneeze? | A germ | A tissue | A cold | *The act or sound of sneezing
test: «Sneezing is a reflex: your body does it without you deciding.» What does reflex mean? | *Something your body does without you deciding | A kind of tissue | A loud noise
exam: «Closing your eyes when you sneeze is a reflex; your eyes would not pop out.» Which statement is true? | You must decide to sneeze before it happens | *Sneezing is something your body does without you deciding | Sneezes never make a sound | Your eyes pop out every time you sneeze
